 "topic": "q-simplification",
 "notes": {
  "summary": "Simplification tests BODMAS, laws of indices and surds. These are speed questions: aim for 30 seconds each.",
  "concepts": [
   {
    "title": "BODMAS",
    "body": "Order: <b>B</b>rackets → <b>O</b>f → <b>D</b>ivision and <b>M</b>ultiplication (left to right) → <b>A</b>ddition and <b>S</b>ubtraction (left to right)."
   },
   {
    "title": "Laws of indices",
    "body": "a<sup>m</sup> × a<sup>n</sup> = a<sup>m+n</sup>; a<sup>m</sup> ÷ a<sup>n</sup> = a<sup>m−n</sup>; (a<sup>m</sup>)<sup>n</sup> = a<sup>mn</sup>; a<sup>0</sup> = 1; a<sup>−n</sup> = 1/a<sup>n</sup>."
   },
   {
    "title": "Surds",
    "body": "To remove a root from the denominator, multiply by the <b>conjugate</b>: 1/(√a + √b) = (√a − √b)/(a − b). To compare roots, raise all to the LCM of the root orders."
   }
  ],
  "varieties": [
   {
    "type": "bodmas",
    "name": "BODMAS",
    "how": "Solve brackets first, then ÷ and × from left to right, then + and −.",
    "example": {
     "q": "Simplify 20 − 12 ÷ 4 × 2.",
     "steps": [
      "12 ÷ 4 = 3",
      "3 × 2 = 6",
      "20 − 6 = 14"
     ],
     "answer": "14"
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "indices",
    "name": "Indices and exponent equations",
    "how": "Bring both sides to the same base, then equate powers.",
    "example": {
     "q": "If 3<sup>x</sup> = 81, find x.",
     "steps": [
      "81 = 3<sup>4</sup>",
      "x = 4"
     ],
     "answer": "4"
    }
   },
   {
    "type": "surds",
    "name": "Surds and comparison",
    "how": "Rationalise using the conjugate; for comparison, raise to a common power.",
    "example": {
     "q": "Rationalise 1/(√5 − √3).",
     "steps": [
      "Multiply by (√5 + √3)/(√5 + √3)",
      "Denominator = 5 − 3 = 2",
      "= (√5 + √3)/2"
     ],
     "answer": "(√5 + √3)/2"
    }
   }
  ],
  "tips": [
   "Division and multiplication have equal priority: go left to right.",
   "For infinite roots √(a + √(a + …)), solve x² = a + x."
  ],
  "traps": [
   "18 ÷ 3 × 2 is 12, not 3.",
   "(a + b)<sup>2</sup> ≠ a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup>, and √(a + b) ≠ √a + √b."
  ]
 },
 "formulas": [
  {
   "name": "Product of powers",
   "expr": "a^m × a^n = a^(m+n)"
  },
  {
   "name": "Power of power",
   "expr": "(a^m)^n = a^(mn)"
  },
  {
   "name": "Rationalise",
   "expr": "1/(√a + √b) = (√a − √b)/(a − b)"
  },
  {
   "name": "Infinite nested root",
   "expr": "√(a + √(a + …)) = x where x² − x − a = 0"
  }
 ],
